{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "05", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "23", "M": "25", "S": "54"}}, "news": [{"title": "South Bengaluru. Experience the finer way of living", "para": "Shriram Properties Ltd is making significant strides in Bengaluru\u2019s southern corridor by developing residential projects that emphasize community living. With 52 projects already delivered and plans for 41 more, the area is witnessing a surge in residential demand. Enhanced connectivity via NICE Road, alongside a strong educational infrastructure, attracts families and professionals alike. Anticipated future developments, including a new airport, are poised to further elevate the region's appeal.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/brand-connect-initiative/south-bengaluru-experience-the-finer-way-of-living/134711597?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-71668/134711597.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "brand-connect-initiative"}, {"title": "Odisha proposes inclusion of 28 more ULBs in PMAY 2.0", "para": "The Odisha government is set to enhance the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana-Urban by adding 28 more urban local bodies, aiming for comprehensive coverage across all 100 urban areas in the state. This initiative will facilitate housing assistance for numerous households, as executive officers are tasked with determining eligible beneficiaries and conducting groundwork for smooth implementation. Verification will focus on housing adequacy and income criteria for families in urban poverty.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/odisha-proposes-inclusion-of-28-more-ulbs-in-pmay-2-0/134685723?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-30522/134685723.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Ambuja Neotia Group to restructure businesses for external funding; IPO a long-term possibility", "para": "Ambuja Neotia Group is consolidating and restructuring entities within the group to create a structure capable of receiving institutional capital, chairman Harshavardhan Neotia said. The exercise is expected to take six-nine months, while the group continues to invest around \u20b92,000 crore annually and plans three project launches in the current financial year.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/ambuja-neotia-group-to-restructure-businesses-for-external-funding-ipo-a-long-term-possibility/134685838?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-93362/134685838.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}